  "body": "(Via https://github.com/jsdom/jsdom/pull/2388)\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-output-element\r\n\r\n> Whenever the element's descendants are changed in any way, if the value mode flag is in mode default, the element's default value must be set to the value of the element's textContent IDL attribute\\.\r\n\r\nIn https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2766 we switched textarea from \"descendant text content\" (= textContent IDL attribute value) to \"child text content\". We also created the well-defined \"child text content changed\" steps.\r\n\r\nIf we made a similar switch, we could rewrite this to be much better grounded in primitives:\r\n\r\n> The [child text content change steps] for the element are to, if the [value mode flag] is in mode [_default_], set the element's [default value] to the element's [child text content].\r\n\r\nHowever, we need to do some browser testing to see whether browsers use child or descendant text contents. If they all use descendants, then maybe we need to try to create a whole \"descendant text content\" and \"descendant text content changed\" steps infrastructure to ground those things well as well.",
